{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774722,"nonce":"tUtKCtvsEQrTVwVc+6SvZCVgJ6k=","title":"feat: searchable ref picker + RepoView run filters (git-bug 4c27eac)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #43 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/ref-picker-and-run-filters` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-20T07:46:49Z · Merged: 2026-07-20T07:49:05Z\n\nCloses both halves of git-bug **4c27eac**.\n\nThe Run-pipeline ref field was free-text only: you had to type an exact branch/tag/SHA, with no way to browse a repo's refs. Root cause was that no backend endpoint enumerated refs.\n\n- **`scarab-forge`**: new `ForgeRef`/`RefKind` types + `ForgePort::list_refs(repo, query)` capability + a shared `filter_refs` helper (case-insensitive substring). Contract suite extended with a `known_branch` assertion (branch surfaces, query narrows).\n- **Adapters**: GitHub (`/branches`+`/tags` via `get_paginated`), Forgejo (paged, tolerates `commit.id` vs `commit.sha`), `RegistryForge` delegate, and `FakeForge` (`with_branch`/`with_tag`).\n- **`scarab-server`**: `GET /v1/repos/{org}/{repo}/refs?q=` → `RefsResponse`/`RefDto` (branches before tags, name-sorted, short SHAs); route + OpenAPI registered.\n- **web-ui**: the free-text ref input becomes a live-filtered combobox (keyboard nav, branch/tag rows, short SHA per row, \"type a full SHA to pin\" hint). Degrades to plain text entry when no forge is configured (`listRefs` returns `[]`).\n\nRestores the author/branch/PR filters removed in the ADR-0054 de-mock, now that `RunSummaryDto` carries provenance (ADR-0046/0049) — no backend change.\n\n- author / branch / PR-number filters from distinct present values, combined with the status pills, plus a clear button.\n- Sparse origin fields honored: a disengaged filter never hides a row; an engaged one excludes rows it can't classify; a filter with no present values hides entirely.\n\nThe native `\u003cselect\u003e`s had no type-ahead — painful once a repo has many branches/authors, and the pattern recurs across the app.\n\n- New `ui/scarab-web-ui/src/components/SearchSelect.tsx`: a searchable single-select — trigger + a **portalled, fixed-positioned** popover with a search box and live-filtered, keyboard-navigable options. Portalled specifically so it's never clipped by an ancestor's `overflow:hidden` (the recurring dropdown-clip trap — which also bit the ref-picker combobox, fixed here too).\n- Adopted for the RepoView author/branch/PR filters and the RunPipeline `choice` param.\n\n- `cargo test --workspace`: **442 passed, 17 live-gated ignored**. web-ui typecheck + build clean. OpenAPI + web-ui `schema.ts` regenerated.\n- **Live against real GitHub** (`thulasi-ram/scarab-ci` on the colima dogfood cluster): `/refs` returns real branches sorted; `?q` filtering incl. case-insensitive + mid-name + no-match. Ref-picker combobox and the searchable filters (search + select + clear) verified in-browser; stack rebuilt + redeployed so the in-cluster UI matches.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}